  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Position Paper on Sustainable Cocoa Sector Development in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Multi-Annual Country Strategy (MACS 2023-2026) by the Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands (EKN) in Ghana focuses on cocoa as a key area for sustainable trade, investments, and development. The Netherlands aims to coordinate and advocate for necessary reforms within the cocoa sector, collaborating with the EU and other partners. The EKN plans to gather input from key stakeholders to influence these reforms, especially as 2024 is an election year in Ghana. 
 The consultant will work  with  partners to solicit their inputs and consolidate them into a position paper. This paper will suggest areas of prioritization for policy focus in the cocoa sector. It will serve as a base document to inform the EKN of the areas of consensus for reforms necessary to achieve a sustainable cocoa sector. It will also be used to engage political parties and  other relevant stakeholders to push for the needed sectoral change.</narrative>
  </description>
